{
  "info": {
    "name": "CockroachDB Mock API 23.2",
    "description": "Test collection for the mock CockroachDB HTTP service. Base URL defaults to http://localhost:8112. In docker-compose, the service is reachable at http://cockroachdb-api:8112. Statements are executed by a real SQL engine and reported with PostgreSQL SQLSTATE codes, because CockroachDB speaks the PostgreSQL wire protocol. Distributed behaviour is modelled: transactions are SERIALIZABLE and a batch touching the seeded contended device row fails its first attempt with 40001 unless max_retries is set; AS OF SYSTEM TIME reads the snapshot taken at process start, so it differs from a live read after a write. The X-CRDB-User header selects the SQL user: root, orbit_app (default), orbit_readonly, orbit_fleet_admin, orbit_changefeed (NOLOGIN).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8112"
    }
  ],
